<span id="S3.T1.9.1.10.9.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center"><span id="S3.T1.9.1.10.9.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFCC;">148.2<span id="S3.T1.9.1.10.9.2.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (<span id="S3.T1.9.1.10.9.2.1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;">148.2<math id="S3.T1.m64" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFCC;" mathbackground="#FFFFCC" mathcolor="#FF8000">×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math></span>)</span></span></span></span>
</span></span><span id="S3.T1.9.1.10.9.3" class="ltx_text"></span></td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.2 Main Results ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ Flash-dLLM: IO-Aware KV Caching and Parallel Decoding for Fast, Memory-Efficient Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> compares the accuracy and decoding efficiency of the evaluated KV-caching and parallel decoding on mathematical reasoning and code-generation benchmarks.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Throughput.</span>
Flash-Cache substantially accelerates greedy decoding, yielding speedups of <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="8.0\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>8.0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8.0\times</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="58.5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>58.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">58.5\times</annotation></semantics></math>. Under confidence-aware decoding, the range increases to <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="17.0\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>17.0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">17.0\times</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="102.2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>102.2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">102.2\times</annotation></semantics></math>, indicating that cache acceleration remains effective with parallel decoding. Combining Flash-Verify and Flash-Cache achieves the highest throughput in all eight settings, reaching <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="148.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>148.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">148.0</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="210.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>210.6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">210.6</annotation></semantics></math> tokens/s and speedups of <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="22.3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>22.3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">22.3\times</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S3.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="148.2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>148.2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">148.2\times</annotation></semantics></math>. Relative to confidence-aware Flash-Cache, the second-fastest configuration throughout, it improves throughput by approximately <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="23.5\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>23.5</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">23.5\%</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S3.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="45.0\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>45.0</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">45.0\%</annotation></semantics></math>. The gains are larger at longer generation lengths: from 256 to 512 tokens, the speedup increases from <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="29.1\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>29.1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">29.1\times</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="81.0\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>81.0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">81.0\times</annotation></semantics></math> on GSM8K, <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="22.3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>22.3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">22.3\times</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="42.0\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>42.0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">42.0\times</annotation></semantics></math> on MATH, <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="29.9\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>29.9</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">29.9\times</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="58.0\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>58.0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">58.0\times</annotation></semantics></math> on HumanEval, and <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="61.7\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>61.7</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">61.7\times</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="148.2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>148.2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">148.2\times</annotation></semantics></math> on MBPP.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Accuracy.</span>
Accuracy exhibits a task-dependent trade-off. On GSM8K-512, Flash-Verify with Flash-Cache achieves both the highest accuracy (<math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="83.02\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>83.02</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">83.02\%</annotation></semantics></math>) and throughput (<math id="S3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="210.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>210.6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">210.6</annotation></semantics></math> tokens/s). Elsewhere, the fastest configuration is not consistently the most accurate: Flash-Verify without caching performs best on GSM8K-256 and MATH-512, whereas confidence-aware Flash-Cache leads on HumanEval-512 and both MBPP settings. On mathematical reasoning tasks, the combined method remains within <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.78" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.78</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.78</annotation></semantics></math> percentage points of the best accuracy. Larger gaps arise for 256-token code generation, reaching <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.66" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3.66</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.66</annotation></semantics></math> points on HumanEval and <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.60" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3.60</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.60</annotation></semantics></math> points on MBPP. Overall, Flash-Verify with Flash-Cache provides the strongest throughput-oriented configuration.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S3.T2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S3.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison of accuracy and decoding throughput across different methods.</span></figcaption>
