<section id="Ax1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A </span>Limitations</h3>

<div id="Ax1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Flash-dLLM is evaluated on two representative masked diffusion LLMs across mathematical reasoning and code generation tasks. While the fused Triton kernel and Flash-Verify are architecture-agnostic in design, we have not yet validated them on continuous-space diffusion language models, where the cache update patterns may differ. Similarly, our benchmarks focus on structured-output tasks; the behavior of confidence-aware decoding on open-ended generation (e.g., long-form writing or dialogue), where token-level confidence distributions tend to be flatter, is an interesting direction for future work. The hyperparameters <math id="Ax1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> are fixed throughout generation; an adaptive scheme that adjusts these based on running confidence statistics could further improve the throughput-accuracy trade-off. We view these as natural extensions and a potential future research direction.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ax1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B </span>Broader Impact</h3>

<div id="Ax1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This work targets inference-time efficiency for diffusion LLMs and does not introduce new training data, model architectures, or fine-tuning procedures. By reducing the computational and memory cost of dLLM decoding, Flash-dLLM lowers the hardware barrier to deploying these models, which could broaden access to non-autoregressive language generation for researchers and practitioners with limited GPU resources. Faster inference also reduces the energy consumption per generated sequence, contributing to more sustainable deployment of large language models. We do not modify safety filters or alignment mechanisms of the underlying models; the generation quality and any associated risks (e.g., producing harmful or biased content) are inherited from the base dLLM. We encourage users to apply standard content moderation and human oversight when deploying Flash-dLLM in user-facing applications, particularly in high-stakes domains.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ax1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C </span>Bounded-Deviation Guarantee for Flash-Verify</h3>

<section id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup.</h4>

<div id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first fix the two distributions that Flash-Verify evaluates at a search
position, following the draft and verify passes of
Section <a href="#S2.SS3" title="2.3 Flash-Verify: KV-cache-driven draft-and-verify Parallel Decoding ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Flash-dLLM: IO-Aware KV Caching and Parallel Decoding for Fast, Memory-Efficient Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>, Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Flash-dLLM: IO-Aware KV Caching and Parallel Decoding for Fast, Memory-Efficient Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and
Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Scheduled flash attention. ‣ 2.2 Flash-Cache: IO-aware key-value caching ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Flash-dLLM: IO-Aware KV Caching and Parallel Decoding for Fast, Memory-Efficient Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Throughout, the quantity being controlled is
the gap between committing several positions at once and committing them from
the model’s own chain-rule joint; this gap is the standard error term of
parallel unmasking in masked diffusion
models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>, <a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, <a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Draft pass.</em> At denoising step <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the draft pass runs the model on the
query set <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Q}^{t}=\mathcal{T}^{t}\cup\mathcal{M}^{t}_{\beta_{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>∪</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Q}^{t}=\mathcal{T}^{t}\cup\mathcal{M}^{t}_{\beta_{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> with every
position in <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{t}_{\beta_{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{t}_{\beta_{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> held at <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\mathrm{MASK}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\mathrm{MASK}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>
denote this input sequence. For each <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{M}^{t}_{\beta_{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{M}^{t}_{\beta_{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> the draft
pass yields the draft-pass distribution over the vocabulary <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, which we
call the <em id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">draft marginal</em></p>
<table id="Ax1.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}(x):=p_{\theta}\!\big(x^{i}=x\mid\mathbf{x}^{t}\big),\qquad x\in V," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}(x):=p_{\theta}\!\big(x^{i}=x\mid\mathbf{x}^{t}\big),\qquad x\in V,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">from which the draft prediction and its confidence are
<math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}^{i}=\arg\max_{x}q_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}^{i}=\arg\max_{x}q_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{i}=q_{i}(\hat{x}^{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{i}=q_{i}(\hat{x}^{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. The window is
partitioned by confidence into the confident set
<math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}^{t}=\{i:c^{i}\geq\epsilon\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}^{t}=\{i:c^{i}\geq\epsilon\}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is accepted directly, and the
search set <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}^{t}=\mathcal{M}^{t}_{\beta_{m}}\setminus\mathcal{D}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>∖</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}^{t}=\mathcal{M}^{t}_{\beta_{m}}\setminus\mathcal{D}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,
which is sent to verification. Note that <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> conditions on no other prediction
made at step <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>: every position in <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{t}_{\beta_{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{t}_{\beta_{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>, including
<math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and the other search positions, is masked in <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Committing <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> directly is covered by the analysis of confidence-aware
decoding <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>, Thm. 1]</cite>: if <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> positions all have marginal
confidence above <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n+1)\varepsilon\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n+1)\varepsilon\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the joint mode
equals the product-of-marginals mode and the two distributions are within
<math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{3n-1}{2}\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{3n-1}{2}\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> in total variation. That result says nothing about
<math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, whose positions fail the confidence condition by construction,
and it is for those positions that the verify pass and the guarantee below are
needed.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Verify pass.</em> Let <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{t}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{t}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> denote <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with the confident
positions committed to their drafts, <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\mathcal{D}^{t}}=\hat{x}^{\mathcal{D}^{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\mathcal{D}^{t}}=\hat{x}^{\mathcal{D}^{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>;
together with the previously decoded tokens this forms the tracked context
<math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>. Write the search positions in causality order (draft
confidence, descending) as <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{1},\dots,i_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{1},\dots,i_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=|\mathcal{S}^{t}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=|\mathcal{S}^{t}|</annotation></semantics></math>. The
verify query duplicates <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> into a <em id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">draft view</em>, filled with
<math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}^{\mathcal{S}^{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}^{\mathcal{S}^{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and a <em id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">mask view</em>, filled with <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\mathrm{MASK}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\mathrm{MASK}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under the causal verify mask of Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Flash-dLLM: IO-Aware KV Caching and Parallel Decoding for Fast, Memory-Efficient Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, the mask view at
<math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> attends to <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>, to the draft view at <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{1},\dots,i_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{1},\dots,i_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and
to the mask view at <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{k},\dots,i_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{k},\dots,i_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>; it does not attend to the draft view at
<math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> or at any later position. Every search position therefore enters its
context exactly once, as a draft if it precedes <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and as <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\mathrm{MASK}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\mathrm{MASK}]</annotation></semantics></math>
otherwise, so the model output at the mask view of <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the mask-view
distribution, which we call the <em id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">verify conditional</em></p>
<table id="Ax1.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i_{k}}(x):=p_{\theta}\!\big(x^{i_{k}}=x\mid\mathbf{x}^{t}_{+},\ \hat{x}^{i_{1}},\dots,\hat{x}^{i_{k-1}}\big),\qquad x\in V," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i_{k}}(x):=p_{\theta}\!\big(x^{i_{k}}=x\mid\mathbf{x}^{t}_{+},\ \hat{x}^{i_{1}},\dots,\hat{x}^{i_{k-1}}\big),\qquad x\in V,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">i.e. the model’s prediction for <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> when the positions before it in
causality order are committed to their drafts and <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{k},\dots,i_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{k},\dots,i_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> remain
masked. This is exactly the input that sequential decoding in this order would
present at its <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th step, and it is the same object that speculative decoding
verifies against: the target model’s conditional at a drafted position given
the accepted tokens before
it <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, <a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>]</cite>.
The mask-view prediction and confidence are
<math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{x}^{i}=\arg\max_{x}p_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{x}^{i}=\arg\max_{x}p_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{c}^{i}=p_{i}(\tilde{x}^{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{c}^{i}=p_{i}(\tilde{x}^{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Flash-Verify accepts position <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> according to</p>
<table id="Ax1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax1.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{accept}(i)=\mathbb{I}\!\big[\hat{x}^{i}=\tilde{x}^{i}\big]\cdot\mathbb{I}\!\big[\tilde{c}^{i}\geq\gamma\big]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>accept</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.219em;" width="0.219em"><mi>𝕀</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mpadded style="width:0.219em;" width="0.219em"><mi>𝕀</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{accept}(i)=\mathbb{I}\!\big[\hat{x}^{i}=\tilde{x}^{i}\big]\cdot\mathbb{I}\!\big[\tilde{c}^{i}\geq\gamma\big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">applied in causality order and stopped at the first rejection, so the
committed block is the longest prefix <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}=\{i_{1},\dots,i_{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}=\{i_{1},\dots,i_{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math> on
which every position is accepted. An accepted token is simultaneously the mode
of the draft marginal <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and a <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-confident mode of the verify
conditional <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. On acceptance the model commits the agreed token, and we
write the delivered distribution at position <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> as the point mass
<math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m29" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{i}(x):=\mathbb{I}[x=\tilde{x}^{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{i}(x):=\mathbb{I}[x=\tilde{x}^{i}]</annotation></semantics></math>. For two distributions <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v</annotation></semantics></math> over a
finite set, total variation distance is
<math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}(u,v):=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{x}|u(x)-v(x)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}(u,v):=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{x}|u(x)-v(x)|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 1</span></span><span id="Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The reference for the committed block is the model’s own sequential
distribution in causality order: at position <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> it is the verify conditional
<math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> of Eq. (<a href="#Ax1.E4" title="In Setup. ‣ C Bounded-Deviation Guarantee for Flash-Verify ‣ Appendix ‣ Flash-dLLM: IO-Aware KV Caching and Parallel Decoding for Fast, Memory-Efficient Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), and over the block it is the
chain-rule joint
<math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{A}}(x^{i_{1}},\dots,x^{i_{m}}):=\prod_{k=1}^{m}p_{\theta}\!\big(x^{i_{k}}\mid\mathbf{x}^{t}_{+},x^{i_{1}},\dots,x^{i_{k-1}}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{A}}(x^{i_{1}},\dots,x^{i_{m}}):=\prod_{k=1}^{m}p_{\theta}\!\big(x^{i_{k}}\mid\mathbf{x}^{t}_{+},x^{i_{1}},\dots,x^{i_{k-1}}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>,
which is the distribution one-token-per-step decoding of the same positions in
the same order samples from. Deviation is measured against this model
distribution rather than the data distribution.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Per-token deviation)<span id="Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ Setup. ‣ C Bounded-Deviation Guarantee for Flash-Verify ‣ Appendix ‣ Flash-dLLM: IO-Aware KV Caching and Parallel Decoding for Fast, Memory-Efficient Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, for every <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}(\pi_{i},p_{i})=1-\tilde{c}^{i}\leq 1-\gamma." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}(\pi_{i},p_{i})=1-\tilde{c}^{i}\leq 1-\gamma.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m:=\tilde{x}^{i}=\arg\max_{x}p_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>:=</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m:=\tilde{x}^{i}=\arg\max_{x}p_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}(m)=\tilde{c}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}(m)=\tilde{c}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{i}(x)=\mathbb{I}[x=m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{i}(x)=\mathbb{I}[x=m]</annotation></semantics></math>. By the definition of total variation,</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}(\pi_{i},p_{i})=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{x\in V}\big|\pi_{i}(x)-p_{i}(x)\big|=\tfrac{1}{2}\Big(\big|\pi_{i}(m)-p_{i}(m)\big|+\sum_{x\neq m}\big|\pi_{i}(x)-p_{i}(x)\big|\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}(\pi_{i},p_{i})=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{x\in V}\big|\pi_{i}(x)-p_{i}(x)\big|=\tfrac{1}{2}\Big(\big|\pi_{i}(m)-p_{i}(m)\big|+\sum_{x\neq m}\big|\pi_{i}(x)-p_{i}(x)\big|\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">At <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=m</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{i}(m)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{i}(m)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, hence
<math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\pi_{i}(m)-p_{i}(m)|=1-p_{i}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\pi_{i}(m)-p_{i}(m)|=1-p_{i}(m)</annotation></semantics></math>. At every <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\neq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\neq m</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{i}(x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{i}(x)=0</annotation></semantics></math>,
hence <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\pi_{i}(x)-p_{i}(x)|=p_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\pi_{i}(x)-p_{i}(x)|=p_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, and since <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a probability
distribution, <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{x\neq m}p_{i}(x)=1-p_{i}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{x\neq m}p_{i}(x)=1-p_{i}(m)</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining,</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}(\pi_{i},p_{i})=\tfrac{1}{2}\big[(1-p_{i}(m))+(1-p_{i}(m))\big]=1-p_{i}(m)=1-\tilde{c}^{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}(\pi_{i},p_{i})=\tfrac{1}{2}\big[(1-p_{i}(m))+(1-p_{i}(m))\big]=1-p_{i}(m)=1-\tilde{c}^{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">The acceptance rule fires only when <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{c}^{i}\geq\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{c}^{i}\geq\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, therefore
<math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}(\pi_{i},p_{i})=1-\tilde{c}^{i}\leq 1-\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}(\pi_{i},p_{i})=1-\tilde{c}^{i}\leq 1-\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmcorollary1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmcorollary1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 1</span></span><span id="Thmcorollary1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Block deviation)<span id="Thmcorollary1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmcorollary1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}=\{i_{1},\dots,i_{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}=\{i_{1},\dots,i_{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the block committed by a single
verify pass, <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathcal{A}}:=\prod_{k=1}^{m}\pi_{i_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathcal{A}}:=\prod_{k=1}^{m}\pi_{i_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> the delivered
distribution over <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> the chain-rule joint of
Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ Setup. ‣ C Bounded-Deviation Guarantee for Flash-Verify ‣ Appendix ‣ Flash-dLLM: IO-Aware KV Caching and Parallel Decoding for Fast, Memory-Efficient Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Then</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}(\pi_{\mathcal{A}},p_{\mathcal{A}})=1-\prod_{k=1}^{m}\tilde{c}^{\,i_{k}}\leq 1-\gamma^{m}\leq m\,(1-\gamma)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}(\pi_{\mathcal{A}},p_{\mathcal{A}})=1-\prod_{k=1}^{m}\tilde{c}^{\,i_{k}}\leq 1-\gamma^{m}\leq m\,(1-\gamma).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Every accepted token equals its draft, <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{x}^{i_{k}}=\hat{x}^{i_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{x}^{i_{k}}=\hat{x}^{i_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the point mass at <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}^{\mathcal{A}}=(\hat{x}^{i_{1}},\dots,\hat{x}^{i_{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}^{\mathcal{A}}=(\hat{x}^{i_{1}},\dots,\hat{x}^{i_{m}})</annotation></semantics></math>. The computation in the proof of
Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Per-token deviation). ‣ Setup. ‣ C Bounded-Deviation Guarantee for Flash-Verify ‣ Appendix ‣ Flash-dLLM: IO-Aware KV Caching and Parallel Decoding for Fast, Memory-Efficient Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> applies verbatim to any point mass <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> and any
distribution <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> on a finite set and gives <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}(\delta_{z},p)=1-p(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}(\delta_{z},p)=1-p(z)</annotation></semantics></math>;
hence <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}(\pi_{\mathcal{A}},p_{\mathcal{A}})=1-p_{\mathcal{A}}(\hat{x}^{\mathcal{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}(\pi_{\mathcal{A}},p_{\mathcal{A}})=1-p_{\mathcal{A}}(\hat{x}^{\mathcal{A}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Evaluating the chain rule at
<math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}^{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}^{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th factor is
<math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(\hat{x}^{i_{k}}\mid\mathbf{x}^{t}_{+},\hat{x}^{i_{1}},\dots,\hat{x}^{i_{k-1}})=p_{i_{k}}(\hat{x}^{i_{k}})=p_{i_{k}}(\tilde{x}^{i_{k}})=\tilde{c}^{\,i_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\hat{x}^{i_{k}}\mid\mathbf{x}^{t}_{+},\hat{x}^{i_{1}},\dots,\hat{x}^{i_{k-1}})=p_{i_{k}}(\hat{x}^{i_{k}})=p_{i_{k}}(\tilde{x}^{i_{k}})=\tilde{c}^{\,i_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> by
Eq. (<a href="#Ax1.E4" title="In Setup. ‣ C Bounded-Deviation Guarantee for Flash-Verify ‣ Appendix ‣ Flash-dLLM: IO-Aware KV Caching and Parallel Decoding for Fast, Memory-Efficient Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>); the conditioning tokens <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}^{i_{1}},\dots,\hat{x}^{i_{k-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}^{i_{1}},\dots,\hat{x}^{i_{k-1}}</annotation></semantics></math> all lie in the accepted prefix, so no rejected draft enters
any factor. Thus <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{A}}(\hat{x}^{\mathcal{A}})=\prod_{k}\tilde{c}^{\,i_{k}}\geq\gamma^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{A}}(\hat{x}^{\mathcal{A}})=\prod_{k}\tilde{c}^{\,i_{k}}\geq\gamma^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\gamma^{m}\leq m(1-\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\gamma^{m}\leq m(1-\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> by Bernoulli’s inequality.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 1</span></span><span id="Thmremark1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(What the reference is)<span id="Thmremark1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Because the verify mask is causal in causality order, <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the
model’s genuine joint over the block, not a product of marginals: the verified
tokens incur no parallel-unmasking dependence error, and the bound is an
equality in the mask-view confidences. The dependence term bounded in KL
by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> and in total variation
by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite> therefore concerns only <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is
committed from marginals and handled by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>, Thm. 1]</cite>. Stopping
at the first rejection is what keeps <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> a prefix, so that every
conditional in <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> conditions only on accepted tokens.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 2</span></span><span id="Thmremark2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Why <math id="Thmremark2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> gates the mask view)<span id="Thmremark2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The bound is controlled by <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> because acceptance thresholds the
confidence of <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the distribution the token is actually committed from.
The confidence threshold <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> instead gates <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{i}=q_{i}(\hat{x}^{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{i}=q_{i}(\hat{x}^{i})</annotation></semantics></math>,
computed with all of <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{t}_{\beta_{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{t}_{\beta_{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> masked <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>;
<math id="Thmremark2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> ignores the other positions decoded in the same step, so <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> can
be its mode yet carry little mass under <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and for a search token
<math id="Thmremark2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{i}&lt;\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{i}&lt;\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> by construction. Hence lowering <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is not equivalent to
verifying: only the latter carries the <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> guarantee against <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. In
the language of speculative decoding, the rule is a deterministic, biased
acceptance <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>]</cite>: the agreement test alone is lossless
with respect to greedy decoding from <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, as in the auto-speculative verifier
of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>, while <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> trades a bounded distribution
bias of <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\tilde{c}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\tilde{c}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for more accepted tokens, the trade-off swept in
Figure <a href="#S3.F5.sf1" title="In Figure 5 ‣ 3.3 Ablation Studies and Analysis ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ Flash-dLLM: IO-Aware KV Caching and Parallel Decoding for Fast, Memory-Efficient Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5(a)</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Ax1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D </span>Detailed Experiment Setup</h3>

<div id="Ax1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Ax1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Implementation Details.</span> All experiments run on a single NVIDIA A100 80GB GPU. We evaluate <span id="Ax1.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Flash-dLLM</span> on LLaDA-1.5 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite> across GSM8K <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>, MATH <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>, HumanEval <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>, and MBPP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>. We implement the fused KV-cache kernel in Triton 2.0. Default benchmark is GSM8K, with default hyperparameters: confidence threshold <math id="Ax1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, verify threshold <math id="Ax1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.8</annotation></semantics></math>, block size <math id="Ax1.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=16</annotation></semantics></math>, tracked budget <math id="Ax1.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}=80" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}=80</annotation></semantics></math>, sliding window size <math id="Ax1.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{m}=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{m}=64</annotation></semantics></math>, generation length 512. For fair comparison, we re-run all baselines under identical hardware and software configurations. <span id="Ax1.SS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baselines.</span> We compare against three approaches: (1) <span id="Ax1.SS4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">No Cache</span>: standard dLLM inference without KV caching, under both greedy (fixed-step) and confidence-aware decoding; (2) <span id="Ax1.SS4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fast-dLLM</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>: prefix-caching with confidence-aware decoding; (3) <span id="Ax1.SS4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Elastic-Cache</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>: adaptive KV caching with attention-pattern-based cache reuse. We report Flash-dLLM results under three configurations: greedy decoding (pure KV-cache speedup), confidence-aware decoding (KV-cache + parallel decoding), and Flash-Verify (KV-cache + draft-and-verify parallel decoding). <span id="Ax1.SS4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evaluation Metrics.</span> We use <span id="Ax1.SS4.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">lm-eval-harness</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>. Throughput is measured as decoding tokens/sec averaged over the benchmark, following Fast-dLLM’s protocol <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>. Accuracy metrics: GSM8K uses 5-shot <span id="Ax1.SS4.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">flexible_extract</span>; MATH uses 4-shot <span id="Ax1.SS4.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">math_verify</span>; HumanEval uses 0-shot <span id="Ax1.SS4.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">pass@1</span> with Fast-dLLM post-processing; MBPP uses 3-shot <span id="Ax1.SS4.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">pass@1</span>. We test at generation lengths 256 and 512 to study scalability.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Ax1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evaluation Framework and Metrics.</span>
Our evaluation protocol comprehensively assesses both inference efficiency and model performance across various tasks. To ensure standardization and reproducibility, we conduct all task-specific evaluations using the <span id="Ax1.SS4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">lm-eval-harness</span> library <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>. Inference speed is measured by throughput in tokens per second (t/s), calculated as the average number of tokens generated by the model over the entire sequence until it produces an end-of-sequence (<span id="Ax1.SS4.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">&lt;eos&gt;</span>) token. We maintain consistency with Fast-dLLM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite> in our calculation methodology to ensure comparable speed benchmarks. Task-specific performance is evaluated using established metrics suitable for each benchmark. For GSM8K <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>, we report 5-shot <span id="Ax1.SS4.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">flexible_extract</span> exact match accuracy. For the MATH dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>, we report the 4-shot <span id="Ax1.SS4.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">math_verify</span> score using the <span id="Ax1.SS4.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">minerva_math</span> variant. For HumanEval <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>, we evaluate 0-shot accuracy using a post-processing script consistent with the Fast-dLLM implementation to ensure fair comparison. Finally, for MBPP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>, we report the 3-shot <span id="Ax1.SS4.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">pass@1</span> metric.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Ax1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hyper-parameters:</span> The hyper-parameters used for Flash-dLLM are presented in Table <a href="#Ax1.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ D Detailed Experiment Setup ‣ Appendix ‣ Flash-dLLM: IO-Aware KV Caching and Parallel Decoding for Fast, Memory-Efficient Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. Specifically,</p>
<ul id="Ax1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ax1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We set the basic block size to <math id="Ax1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=16</annotation></semantics></math>, corresponding to the smallest block used in our Triton implementation.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For confidence-aware decoding, we use <math id="Ax1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, following the optimal setting reported by Fast-dLLM.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use a default masked-window size of <math id="Ax1.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{m}=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{m}=64</annotation></semantics></math> across all settings to balance accuracy and decoding speed.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax1.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax1.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We set <math id="Ax1.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.8</annotation></semantics></math> for GSM8K and MBPP and <math id="Ax1.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.85" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.85</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.85</annotation></semantics></math> for MATH and HumanEval.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax1.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax1.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use a batch size of <math id="Ax1.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>32</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32</annotation></semantics></math> in all experiments to maximize GPU utilization.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="Ax1.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="Ax1.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="Ax1.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The hyper-parameters of Flash-dLLM under various settings.</span></figcaption>
<div id="Ax1.T3.5" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:341.6pt;height:68.3pt;vertical-align:-32.6pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-107.5pt,21.5pt) scale(0.613777838200262,0.613777838200262) ;">
<table id="Ax1.T3.5.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="Ax1.T3.5.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="Ax1.T3.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="Ax1.T3.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></td>
<td id="Ax1.T3.5.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="Ax1.T3.5.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Benchmark</span></td>
<td id="Ax1.T3.5.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="Ax1.T3.5.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gen Length</span></td>
<td id="Ax1.T3.5.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Tracking budget <math id="Ax1.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="Ax1.T3.5.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Window size <math id="Ax1.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="Ax1.T3.5.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Flash-Verify <math id="Ax1.T3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="Ax1.T3.5.1.1.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Batch size</td></tr>
