<div id="Ax1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table  <a href="#Ax1.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ E Statistical analysis ‣ Appendix ‣ Flash-dLLM: IO-Aware KV Caching and Parallel Decoding for Fast, Memory-Efficient Diffusion LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> examines the joint effect of the denoising parameter <math id="Ax1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and track budget <math id="Ax1.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> on accuracy and throughput. The results show a consistent accuracy–efficiency trade-off: increasing either parameter generally improves accuracy while reducing decoding throughput. At a fixed <math id="Ax1.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, increasing <math id="Ax1.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="Ax1.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="48" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>48</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">48</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Ax1.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="96" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>96</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">96</annotation></semantics></math> improves accuracy by approximately <math id="Ax1.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.83" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.83</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.83</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="Ax1.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.69" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.69</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.69</annotation></semantics></math> percentage points, but decreases throughput by about <math id="Ax1.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10.9\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10.9</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10.9\%</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="Ax1.SS5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20.3\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>20.3</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20.3\%</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, increasing <math id="Ax1.SS5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="Ax1.SS5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.60" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.60</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.60</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Ax1.SS5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.00" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.00</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.00</annotation></semantics></math> yields an accuracy gain of <math id="Ax1.SS5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.44" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.44</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.44</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="Ax1.SS5.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.99</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.99</annotation></semantics></math> percentage points across the evaluated track budgets, accompanied by a throughput reduction of approximately <math id="Ax1.SS5.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40.6\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>40.6</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40.6\%</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="Ax1.SS5.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="44.4\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>44.4</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">44.4\%</annotation></semantics></math>. Although a few neighboring configurations exhibit small non-monotonic variations, these differences are generally comparable to the reported standard deviations and do not alter the overall trend.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The highest-throughput configuration is obtained with <math id="Ax1.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.60" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.60</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.60</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax1.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}=48" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}=48</annotation></semantics></math>, reaching <math id="Ax1.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="277.80" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>277.80</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">277.80</annotation></semantics></math> tokens/s at <math id="Ax1.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="80.23\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>80.23</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">80.23\%</annotation></semantics></math> accuracy. In contrast, the highest accuracy of <math id="Ax1.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="83.41\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>83.41</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">83.41\%</annotation></semantics></math> is achieved with <math id="Ax1.SS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=1.00" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.00</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=1.00</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax1.SS5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}=96" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>96</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}=96</annotation></semantics></math>, where throughput decreases to <math id="Ax1.SS5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="131.58" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>131.58</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">131.58</annotation></semantics></math> tokens/s. Thus, moving from the fastest to the most accurate configuration improves accuracy by <math id="Ax1.SS5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.18" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3.18</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.18</annotation></semantics></math> percentage points while reducing throughput by approximately <math id="Ax1.SS5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="52.6\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>52.6</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">52.6\%</annotation></semantics></math>. Intermediate settings provide more balanced operating points. In particular, <math id="Ax1.SS5.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.85" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.85</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.85</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax1.SS5.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}=96" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>96</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}=96</annotation></semantics></math> achieve <math id="Ax1.SS5.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="83.15\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>83.15</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">83.15\%</annotation></semantics></math> accuracy at <math id="Ax1.SS5.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="185.70" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>185.70</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">185.70</annotation></semantics></math> tokens/s, remaining only <math id="Ax1.SS5.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.26" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.26</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.26</annotation></semantics></math> percentage points below the maximum accuracy while providing approximately <math id="Ax1.SS5.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="41.1\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>41.1</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">41.1\%</annotation></semantics></math> higher throughput. The relatively small standard deviations across five random seeds—at most <math id="Ax1.SS5.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.03" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.03</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.03</annotation></semantics></math> percentage points for accuracy and <math id="Ax1.SS5.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4.94" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4.94</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.94</annotation></semantics></math> tokens/s for throughput—also indicate that the observed trade-off is consistent across runs. Overall, <math id="Ax1.SS5.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax1.SS5.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> offer complementary controls for selecting either a throughput-oriented or accuracy-oriented operating point.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ax1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F </span>Ablation of Generation and Prefill Length.</h3>

<figure id="Ax1.T5" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="Ax1.T5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 5</span>: </span><span id="Ax1.T5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Ablation of generation and prefill lengths.</span></figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="Ax1.T5.st1" class="ltx_table ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="Ax1.T5.st1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="Ax1.T5.st1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">Impact of generation length on LLaDA-1.5 for GSM8K (5-shot) with a batch size of 16.</span></figcaption>
<div id="Ax1.T5.st1.7" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:88pt;vertical-align:-42.3pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-3.7pt,0.9pt) scale(0.979190249673176,0.979190249673176) ;">
<table id="Ax1.T5.st1.7.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="Ax1.T5.st1.7.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="Ax1.T5.st1.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.2pt 2.5pt;"><span id="Ax1.T5.st1.7.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">Approach</span></td>
<td id="Ax1.T5.st1.7.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.2pt 2.5pt;"><span id="Ax1.T5.st1.7.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">Metric</span></td>
<td id="Ax1.T5.st1.7.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.2pt 2.5pt;"><span id="Ax1.T5.st1.7.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">Len. 128</span></td>
<td id="Ax1.T5.st1.7.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.2pt 2.5pt;"><span id="Ax1.T5.st1.7.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">Len. 256</span></td>
<td id="Ax1.T5.st1.7.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.2pt 2.5pt;"><span id="Ax1.T5.st1.7.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">Len. 512</span></td>
<td id="Ax1.T5.st1.7.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.2pt 2.5pt;"><span id="Ax1.T5.st1.7.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">Len. 1024</span></td></tr>
<tr id="Ax1.T5.st1.7.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="Ax1.T5.st1.7.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.2pt 2.5pt;" rowspan="3"><span id="Ax1.T5.st1.7.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;"><span id="Ax1.T5.st1.7.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span> <span id="Ax1.T5.st1.7.1.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text">
<span id="Ax1.T5.st1.7.1.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="Ax1.T5.st1.7.1.2.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="Ax1.T5.st1.7.1.2.1.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding:0.2pt 2.5pt;">Flash-Cache</span></span>
